{
  "about": [
    "The tables' natural sort key (coordinator, 21 Oct 2026): one definition, written once in Go (business/RowQuery naturalKey, the cell index's sort column) and once in TypeScript (lib/tables/sortKey.ts, the browser's sorts), each held to this file. It is copied byte for byte into both repositories' testdata/sortkey.",
    "The key: the text in NFKD with its combining marks (Mn) dropped; case-folded (lower case, then ß and ẞ as ss, ς as σ, Cherokee small letters as capitals); trimmed of whitespace at both ends; each run of ASCII digits read as a number, its leading zeros dropped and zero-padded to 20 digits (a run longer than 20 digits is written as ':', its length in two digits, 99 at most, and the run, so it sorts after every padded number, and among such runs by length, then digits); and cut to its first 256 code points, so its index entry always fits (Postgres refuses a btree entry over 2,704 bytes). Keys compare by code point, as Postgres's C collation compares UTF-8.",
    "keys: each input's key. order: the inputs sorted by key, ties kept in the order the keys list them (a stable sort). Empty text has the empty key; the grid sorts blanks last itself."
  ],
